WEBVTT

00:11:59.996 --> 00:12:02.196
The other data that I found
throughout the book

00:12:02.236 --> 00:12:04.556
is that women of color
don't often get feedback,

00:12:04.556 --> 00:12:06.596
Black women especially don't get feedback

00:12:06.636 --> 00:12:08.836
in any sort of level of detail
that's helpful.

00:12:08.876 --> 00:12:10.476
So thank you for sharing that.

00:12:10.476 --> 00:12:11.956
G: Oh, my pleasure.

00:12:11.996 --> 00:12:15.756
DP: I think Gina's example is so beautiful
because the question I get is,

00:12:15.796 --> 00:12:17.196
how do I stand up for myself?

00:12:17.196 --> 00:12:18.916
How can you advocate for yourself

00:12:18.956 --> 00:12:21.716
that isn't going to make people
call you aggressive, right?

00:12:21.716 --> 00:12:23.076
Or too over the top.

00:12:23.116 --> 00:12:26.276
And, you know, in the book,
I called it a little bit of Goldilocks,

00:12:26.316 --> 00:12:27.716
like, you can ask for things,

00:12:27.716 --> 00:12:30.396
but then there's backlash
if you ask for too many things.